  "observations": "PART A. The three LIT-002 fixes are in as opt-in flags (AM_BETA_BOX=3.0, AM_NNLS_ITERS=2, AM_NNLS_DRIVER=gelsd, plus AM_BETA_TARGET) and _should_fit_beta is decoupled from key_mode. With beta off the build is bit-identical: the control arm reproduced EXP-007-top32 / DIAG-ROPE arm A to all 17 in-run digits (QA 2.1766157150268555 / MT 2.5483615398406982, mean_mse_last_doc 0.19807696944925424, |v|max 984.0) and its standalone eval_forgetting QA (2.1771795749664307) / MT (2.5524158477783203) match DIAG-ROPE exactly; unit-level, nnls_projected_gradient and refit_beta_nnls at default arguments are bit-identical to the committed HEAD implementation on both CPU and CUDA. One correction to LIT-002 found on the GPU: torch accepts driver='gelsd' only for CPU inputs and RAISES on CUDA, so the warm start now falls back to a CPU gelsd solve (recorded as warm_start_on_cpu) -- without that the except-RuntimeError branch would have silently used a uniform warm start. PART B. beta executed end-to-end for the first time in this project: 288 fits/document x 16 documents, 0 non-finite warm starts, 0 raised, 10/288 rank-deficient at the last document (lstsq rank 25-32 of 32), all beta finite and inside [-3, 3]. LIT-002 divergence #3 is a non-issue at KEY_MODE=freeze: the residual target (target - fixed_mass) is strictly positive by construction there, and the measured clamp fraction is 5.4e-5. Fitted beta saturates upward -- 59.7% of entries at the +3 ceiling on the last document, per-layer medians 2.22-3.00 across all 36 layers, min -3.0 / max +3.0 everywhere. HEADLINE: eval-time mass_on_S on MT went 0.0711 (rope-only) -> 0.3010, a 4.23x increase and 3.36x Phase-1's 0.0896; every one of the 36 layers rose; total cartridge mass 0.593 -> 0.679. And MT did not improve -- it regressed +0.282 (2.5296 -> 2.8112), ~1.5x the noise band, with QA regressing +0.581 (2.1597 -> 2.7403, past the 2.52 retention budget). The MT/QA mass ratio was 1.0428 without beta and 1.0509 with it (Phase-1 1.0832), i.e. a 4.2x bandwidth gain bought +0.008 of selectivity, matching the prior scout's algebraic prediction of ~1.03-1.05. The solve's own objective improved while CE degraded (mean am/mean_mse 0.01406 -> 0.00782, 1.8x better; |v|max 178 -> 107.5), another instance of the B-OBJ anti-correlation. Cost: solve_s 184.3 -> 241.4 (1.31x), phase2 e2e 304 s, 0 gradient steps. All three arms have wandb runs; control and rope reproduce their references exactly."
